REM APPLESOFT BASIC
10 REM SOFT SWITCHES, POKES INTO THE SCREEN PAGES, AND BLOAD
20 PRINT CHR$ (4);"BLOAD STRIPES"
30 POKE - 16304,0: POKE - 16297,0: POKE - 16300,0: POKE - 16302,0: REM GRAPHICS, HI-RES, PAGE 1, FULL SCREEN
40 REM A BYTE OF FOUR DOTS AT THE START OF EVERY EIGHTH LINE
50 FOR A = 8192 TO 9192 STEP 128: POKE A,85: NEXT
60 HOME : PRINT "A";: INVERSE : PRINT "B";: FLASH : PRINT "C": NORMAL
70 PRINT PEEK (1024);" "; PEEK (1025);" "; PEEK (1026);" "; PEEK (8192);" "; PEEK (16384)
80 POKE 1063,193: REM AN "A" AT THE TOP RIGHT
90 REM AN ONERR HANDLER IS NOT GIVEN WHAT THE INTERPRETER CANNOT DO
100 ONERR GOTO 120
110 POKE 49408,0
120 PRINT "NOT REACHED"
